              "author": "PCP",
              "date": "2021-06-07T09:45",
              "body": "Yearly visit. No admissions since Feb 2020, longest stretch he can remember. Got both COVID shots in April/May. Hip about the same, aches by the end of a library shift on his feet.\nHematology: saw them in the winter, no changes.\nMeds per his report: hydroxyurea 1000 mg daily, penicillin VK 250 BID, folic acid daily.\nNKDA. Never smoker, rare alcohol.\nROS neg.\nExam: well appearing. Lungs clear. Heart regular. Abdomen soft, no masses or organomegaly. R hip end-range IR discomfort. No edema, skin intact.\nPHQ-2 0.\nA/P: HbSS, quiet year. Yearly CBC, CMP, urine albumin. Tdap due (last 2011), given. MenACWY booster given for asplenia, next one 2026. Flu in fall. RTC 6 months for a sickle cell check, sooner if needed."
            }
