          "documents": [
            {
              "type": "Progress Notes",
              "title": "Office Visit - Fatigue",
              "author": "PCP",
              "date": "2021-11-29T14:40",
              "body": "CC: tired, short of breath.\nS: Several weeks of steadily worse fatigue, now winded on one flight of stairs and walking from the bus. No pain crisis in the last 6 months. No fever, cough, chest pain, sick contacts. No bleeding, black stools or blood in urine. Eating the same as always. Taking hydroxyurea and penicillin. Asked about folic acid: \"I think I ran out a while ago.\" Fill history from the pharmacy shows last folic acid fill in March.\nO: Pale. Scleral icterus. Lungs clear, no crackles. Heart regular. Abdomen soft; spleen tip felt about 2 cm below the left costal margin, nontender. No edema.\nA/P\n1. Fatigue and exertional dyspnea, HbSS. More anemic-looking than his baseline, jaundiced. Concern for folate depletion off supplement on top of his hemolysis. CBC, retic, folate, LDH, bili, haptoglobin now.\n2. Palpable spleen, new on our exams. Add splenomegaly to the list, recheck on follow-up.\n3. Folic acid lapsed since spring; off the active list until labs are back, then I will send a new script.\nReturn precautions given: fever, chest pain, worsening SOB, pain crisis = ED."
            },
            {
              "type": "Result note",
              "title": "Same-day CBC",
              "author": "PCP",
              "date": "2021-11-29T16:30",
              "body": "Hgb 7.8 (his usual is low 8s), MCV 102, retic only 1%, LDH 420, total bili 3.1 / direct 0.5. Retic is far lower than his usual 4-10%: marrow not keeping up. Waiting on folate and haptoglobin."
            }
