              "author": "PCP",
              "date": "2022-05-16T10:10",
              "body": "Annual exam.\nSince last year: folate deficiency anemia in Nov after running out of folic acid, repleted, recheck in January normal. Taking it daily now. Energy good. No crises, no admissions. Still at the library and taking classes.\nHematology visit in March, regimen unchanged per pt.\nMeds: hydroxyurea 1000 mg daily, folic acid 1 mg daily, penicillin VK 250 mg BID. NKDA.\nROS: no chest pain, dyspnea, priapism, vision change.\nExam: well. Lungs clear. Heart regular. Abdomen soft, spleen tip just palpable, nontender. R hip unchanged. No leg ulcers.\nPHQ-2 0.\nA/P: HbSS, stable, hemoglobin should settle back near his usual on folate. Splenomegaly, small, unchanged. Annual labs. PCV20 today for asplenia. Hasn't had a sickle cell eye exam since peds; referral to ophthalmology for a dilated exam. Flu and COVID updates in the fall."
